  abstract={In an era of global volatility and interconnected supply chains, the ability to detect and interpret external disruptions is essential for maintaining operational resilience. This paper presents a multimodal, AI-driven framework for the early detection of disruption indicators, designed within the M4ESTRO[1] project to support trusted, explainable, and human-centered Manufacturing-as-a-Service (MaaS) environments. The component integrates real-time sensing from diverse sources-including financial APIs, global news platforms, and social sentiment channels-using explainable AI techniques such as anomaly detection, semantic analysis, and interpretable scoring. These indicators are contextualized within a federated data infrastructure to support proactive reconfiguration and supply chain adaptation. The system promotes transparent decision-making through structured indicators, while also laying the foundation for edge-deployable AI capabilities. This work contributes to the development of trustworthy IoT/AI systems aligned with Industry 5.0 principles, emphasizing explainability, collaboration, and resilience in decentralized industrial ecosystems.},
