  pages={01-08},
  abstract={As the industrial landscape transitions from Industry 4.0 to Industry 5.0, the role of human operators is becoming increasingly central, with a renewed emphasis on balancing efficiency and well-being. Emerging technologies now allow machines to better handle the uncertainty and variability of human behaviour, enabling deeper human-machine collaboration. However, in complex scenarios, workers still need adaptive, context-aware support to perform effectively. Extended Reality technologies offer powerful tools to enhance task execution and training, but they also introduce challenges like visual fatigue, cognitive overload, and reduced user engagement. To address these, adaptive interfaces can tailor Extended Reality environments to individual users, provided that accurate and dynamic user profiles are available. In this work, we introduce a system that integrates Asset Administration Shells and Humancentric Digital Twins to continuously collect environmental and operator-specific data to generate human digital images. The digital images are then used to adapt XR interfaces in real-time, enhancing both user experience and operational performance in human-centred industrial systems.},
