  booktitle={2025 21st International Conference on Distributed Computing in Smart Systems and the Internet of Things (DCOSS-IoT)}, 
  title={Hybrid Predictive Modeling for Single-Sensor Data Consistency in Industrial IoT}, 
  year={2025},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={231-235},
  abstract={Modern Industry 5.0 environments depend on reliable sensor data provided through the Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT) for data-driven control in highly regulated fields like pharmaceuticals. While most state-of-the-art research emphasizes multi-sensor setups for ensuring data consistency, this study focuses on the consistency of data from a single pressure sensor that monitors cyclical process events. Our methodology employs and compares several time-series forecasting models to predict normal valve operation and detect anomalous events. We introduce a hybrid predictive model that combines a deep learning model, trained to capture the short-range dependencies of normal cyclical patterns, with an ARIMA model optimized for forecasting long-term deviations representing anomalies. A quantitative consistency score provides a robust measure of data integrity for single-sensor systems. Experimental results showcase the hybrid model's performance and demonstrate the effectiveness of our framework in anticipating valve behavior.},
